1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
the first time Amara saw Kong Min Jun

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,133
kill a man's entire future

3
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:08,600
she was barefoot in his kitchen wearing his shirt

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,366
drinking coffee from a mug that said

5
00:00:09,366 --> 00:00:12,800
World's okayest husband

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,633
his voice drifted from the study

7
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:17,100
calm as a weather forecast

8
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,166
freeze his accounts all of them

9
00:00:19,166 --> 00:00:21,133
and tell his wife about the mistress

10
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,966
use the photos from Thursday

11
00:00:22,966 --> 00:00:25,166
he hung up padded into the kitchen

12
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:26,200
kissed her forehead

13
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,900
and asked if she wanted pancakes or waffles

14
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,433
she chose waffles she always chose waffles

15
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:34,600
and she tried not to think about the man

16
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,266
whose life had just ended

17
00:00:36,266 --> 00:00:40,000
somewhere between her first and second sip of coffee

18
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
this was her life now penthouse in Gangnam

19
00:00:43,066 --> 00:00:45,300
42nd floor Florida

20
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:45,666
ceiling

21
00:00:45,666 --> 00:00:48,700
windows that turn soul into a glittering circuit board

22
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,800
every night a walk in closet

23
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,200
the size of her old apartment in Atlanta

24
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,466
a husband whose name made powerful men go pale

25
00:00:56,466 --> 00:00:58,866
and still still

26
00:00:59,166 --> 00:01:01,300
Amara reached past the Valentino

27
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,566
past the Dior past the row of silk blouses

28
00:01:04,566 --> 00:01:06,866
that cost more than her first car

29
00:01:06,966 --> 00:01:08,166
and pulled out a plain

30
00:01:08,166 --> 00:01:10,900
black dress she'd bought at a market in Itaewon

31
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,366
two years ago 15,001

32
00:01:13,366 --> 00:01:17,100
about $11 old habits from harder times

33
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,266
you're doing it again

34
00:01:18,266 --> 00:01:20,166
Min June leaned against the door frame

35
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:22,900
already dressed in a charcoal three piece suit

36
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,833
his dark hair pushed back

37
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:27,466
his jaw sharp enough to cut the morning light

38
00:01:27,466 --> 00:01:28,866
slanting through the windows

39
00:01:28,866 --> 00:01:30,900
he looked like a man who owned things

40
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:32,233
buildings companies

41
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:35,433
people he looked like exactly what he was doing

42
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,266
what shopping in your closet

43
00:01:37,266 --> 00:01:39,300
like you're on a budget she smiled

44
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,966
clipping on pearl earrings

45
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,800
a gift from their first anniversary

46
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,600
that she wore almost every day

47
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,400
I like simple things I like spoiling you

48
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,166
he crossed to her his hands finding her waist

49
00:01:50,166 --> 00:01:52,800
with the ease of someone who'd memorized her body

50
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,033
like a map his lips brushed her neck

51
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:56,366
warm deliberate

52
00:01:56,366 --> 00:02:00,566
humor me you humor me by loving me exactly as I am

53
00:02:00,566 --> 00:02:02,433
his expression softened in that way

54
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:06,000
it only did for her the hard edges dissolving

55
00:02:06,033 --> 00:02:08,700
the underground king retreating behind the man

56
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:11,033
he held her gaze for a beat too long

57
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:14,033
and she saw it again that flicker of disbelief

58
00:02:14,033 --> 00:02:16,900
like he still couldn't quite accept that she was real

59
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,466
that she was here that she'd stayed

60
00:02:19,466 --> 00:02:21,133
then more carefully

61
00:02:21,666 --> 00:02:23,800
you're going to Gangnam Mall today

62
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,400
just some Christmas shopping

63
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,366
I won't be long something tightened behind his eyes

64
00:02:28,366 --> 00:02:30,966
take Jin Woo and Taehyung baby

65
00:02:30,966 --> 00:02:34,266
I don't need bodyguards to go Christmas shopping Amara

66
00:02:34,266 --> 00:02:37,133
the softness vanished his jaw locked

67
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,500
his hands still gentle on her waist

68
00:02:39,733 --> 00:02:43,200
but his voice carved from something cold and immovable

69
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,566
you know what I am you know what I do

70
00:02:45,566 --> 00:02:47,400
you know the enemies that creates

71
00:02:47,566 --> 00:02:49,833
you don't leave this house without security

72
00:02:49,833 --> 00:02:52,666
non negotiable there it was

73
00:02:52,966 --> 00:02:56,166
the line where husband ended and king began

74
00:02:56,166 --> 00:02:57,800
she felt it every time

75
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,066
that invisible wall she could press against

76
00:03:00,066 --> 00:03:02,600
but never break through she cupped his face

77
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,066
okay I'll take that

78
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:05,800
the tension left his shoulders

79
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:08,700
he kissed her deep slow

80
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,700
thorough enough to make her forget

81
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,366
what they'd been arguing about

82
00:03:12,566 --> 00:03:15,433
then checked his watch solid platinum simple

83
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:19,166
obscenely expensive I have a meeting home by 7

84
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,066
we have dinner reservations at 8

85
00:03:21,066 --> 00:03:23,233
where that dangerous smile

86
00:03:23,233 --> 00:03:26,333
the one that had made her say yes to a second date

87
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,300
a third a ring

88
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:30,766
a life she never imagined

89
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,833
surprise wear the red dress

90
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:34,033
which red dress

91
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:37,100
the one I can't stop thinking about removing

92
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,800
heat climbed her neck you're insatiable

93
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,100
only for you one more kiss and then he was gone

94
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,866
his Cologne lingering in the air

95
00:03:44,866 --> 00:03:46,700
like a promise and a warning

96
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:48,766
Amara stood alone in their closet

97
00:03:48,766 --> 00:03:49,666
in the silence

98
00:03:49,666 --> 00:03:51,966
she opened the bottom drawer of her vanity

99
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,666
the one minjin never touched

100
00:03:53,666 --> 00:03:55,566
because she'd asked him not to

101
00:03:55,566 --> 00:03:57,200
and he respected her boundaries

102
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,466
even when he respected nothing else

103
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,000
inside a worn leather journal

104
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,900
she didn't open it didn't need to

105
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,800
she knew the last page by heart

106
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,100
$17

107
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,833
that's what I'm worth

108
00:04:08,833 --> 00:04:12,000
$17 and a car that smells like failure

109
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,800
she closed the drawer pressed her palm flat against it

110
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,266
as if holding something down

111
00:04:16,266 --> 00:04:18,333
three years a whole new life

112
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:19,566
a whole new country

113
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:23,400
a whole new name and still that girl lived inside her

114
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:25,700
the one who'd woken up in a pool of blood

115
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,500
on the floor of a charity ward

116
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,433
alone with nothing left

117
00:04:29,433 --> 00:04:32,866
Amara straightened smoothed her eleven dollar dress

118
00:04:32,866 --> 00:04:34,133
checked her reflection

119
00:04:34,266 --> 00:04:36,300
a woman who looked like she had everything

120
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,200
and went Christmas shopping

121
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,266
she saw him before he saw her

122
00:04:40,266 --> 00:04:41,433
Marcus Wellington

123
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:43,233
standing in the Louis Vuitton section

124
00:04:43,233 --> 00:04:46,666
like he belonged there leaning against a display case

125
00:04:46,666 --> 00:04:49,633
laughing with a woman whose entire outfit screamed

126
00:04:49,633 --> 00:04:52,100
new money trying to look like old money

127
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,766
same cocky smile

128
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:57,700
same expensive taste funded by other people's wallets

129
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:59,466
same entitled swagger

130
00:04:59,566 --> 00:05:02,000
that she'd once mistaken for confidence

131
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:04,300
three years three years of rebuilding

132
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,800
of teaching herself to eat without guilt

133
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:10,500
sleep without nightmares trust without flinching

134
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,566
three years of becoming someone new

135
00:05:12,566 --> 00:05:14,600
in a country where no one knew her name

136
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:18,800
or her shame and he was just standing there laughing

137
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,100
her hands trembled

138
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:22,600
the shopping bags nearly slipped from her grip

139
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,166
Jean Woo

140
00:05:23,166 --> 00:05:26,066
and Taiyang flanked her at a respectful distance

141
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:28,500
unaware that the woman they were protecting

142
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,900
had just stopped breathing

143
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,566
walk away turn around

144
00:05:31,566 --> 00:05:34,566
leave but her feet were welded to the marble floor

145
00:05:34,566 --> 00:05:37,000
Marcus looked up their eyes met

146
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,166
one second of nothing she was just another face

147
00:05:40,166 --> 00:05:41,966
in a crowd of wealthy shoppers

148
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,200
and then recognition hit him like a slap

149
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:48,166
shock first then something uglier

150
00:05:48,166 --> 00:05:50,433
something that curdled behind his eyes

151
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,566
and settled into the familiar sneer

152
00:05:52,566 --> 00:05:54,800
she used to cry herself to sleep over

153
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,666
he whispered something to the woman

154
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:58,266
started walking toward her

155
00:05:58,266 --> 00:06:01,400
every nerve in Amara's body screamed run

156
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,700
she didn't well

157
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:05,333
well that voice that tone

158
00:06:05,366 --> 00:06:07,633
condescending as a pat on the head

159
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:10,400
Amara didn't expect to see you here

160
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,966
thought you'd be at the thrift stores where you belong

161
00:06:12,966 --> 00:06:14,900
she found her voice somewhere

162
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:17,966
beneath the rubble of three years of therapy

163
00:06:17,966 --> 00:06:21,100
Marcus I have nothing to say to you

164
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,866
what's wrong still bitter

165
00:06:23,266 --> 00:06:26,733
his eyes traveled over her mocking assessing

166
00:06:26,766 --> 00:06:29,066
dismissing though I see you cleaned up

167
00:06:29,066 --> 00:06:31,366
found some desperate man to pay your bills

168
00:06:31,366 --> 00:06:32,933
that's always been your talent

169
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:36,466
hasn't it playing victim until some fool takes pity

170
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:38,233
Jean Wu moved closer

171
00:06:38,233 --> 00:06:40,166
Taehyung's hand drifted toward his phone

172
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:43,366
you left me with nothing Amara said quietly

173
00:06:43,566 --> 00:06:46,866
and she hated hated how her voice shook

174
00:06:46,866 --> 00:06:49,233
you stole everything I had

175
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:51,866
Marcus laughed loud enough to turn heads

176
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:56,200
stole baby I liberated myself from a parasite

177
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,166
best decision I ever made

178
00:06:58,166 --> 00:06:59,833
I was pregnant with your child

179
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:03,000
and I told you from the beginning I didn't want kids

180
00:07:03,033 --> 00:07:04,966
you probably got pregnant on purpose

181
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:07,766
trying to trap me his eyes were flat dead

182
00:07:07,766 --> 00:07:09,833
not even the decency of cruelty

183
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:13,433
just indifference thank god I got out when I did

184
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,466
the woman on his arm appeared

185
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:17,766
linking herself to him possessively

186
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:20,800
is this her the ex who stalked you

187
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,466
I never don't make a scene

188
00:07:23,466 --> 00:07:26,000
Marcus cut her off already turning to leave

189
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,666
dismissing her again

190
00:07:27,666 --> 00:07:30,000
the way he dismissed her three years ago

191
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,700
with a note on the kitchen counter

192
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:33,266
and an emptied bank account

193
00:07:33,266 --> 00:07:35,166
something cracked inside her chest

194
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:37,066
not broke cracked

195
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,366
the way ice cracks before it gives way completely

196
00:07:40,366 --> 00:07:42,400
you destroyed me she said

197
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,433
and her voice didn't shake this time

198
00:07:44,433 --> 00:07:47,100
I lost our baby because I was starving

199
00:07:47,166 --> 00:07:49,666
homeless sleeping in my car

200
00:07:50,066 --> 00:07:52,200
shut up he spun back

201
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:55,466
face twisted don't you dare guilt me with that

202
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,666
I survived you Marcus

203
00:07:57,666 --> 00:07:59,000
the words came from somewhere

204
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,366
deep and ancient and unbreakable

205
00:08:01,366 --> 00:08:03,200
that's what you can't stand

206
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,666
not that I moved on but that I didn't need you to

207
00:08:06,666 --> 00:08:10,000
his face went red he shoved past Jean Wu

208
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,600
who shifted like a wall

209
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,833
and his hand connected with Amara's shoulder hard

210
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:17,800
she stumbled backward into a display stand ornament

211
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,366
shattering her elbow

212
00:08:19,366 --> 00:08:21,466
splitting open against the metal edge

213
00:08:21,466 --> 00:08:23,766
she hit the ground her dress tore

214
00:08:24,333 --> 00:08:27,333
blood bloomed on her arm the mall went silent

215
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,433
Marcus stood over her chest

216
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:31,300
heaving fist still clenched

217
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,766
stay down where you belong

218
00:08:32,766 --> 00:08:33,966
you worthless

219
00:08:34,566 --> 00:08:35,666
he didn't finish

220
00:08:35,666 --> 00:08:38,066
Jin Woo had him on the ground in two seconds

221
00:08:38,066 --> 00:08:40,633
flat arm twisted behind his back

222
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:43,033
Taehyung was already pulling Amara to her feet

223
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:44,200
with one hand

224
00:08:44,233 --> 00:08:46,433
his phone pressed to his ear with the other

225
00:08:46,433 --> 00:08:49,033
his face had gone the color of ash

226
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:52,066
not fear for himself fear for what was coming

227
00:08:52,066 --> 00:08:54,500
because Min jong was going to find out

228
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,533
and when Kong Min jong found out

229
00:08:56,566 --> 00:08:58,900
the world had a way of catching fire

230
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:01,600
Taiyang spoke rapid Korean into the phone

231
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:05,100
too fast for Amara's intermediate skills to follow

232
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,900
then handed it to her his hand was shaking

233
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,500
hello her voice came out

234
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:12,066
small silence on the other end

235
00:09:12,066 --> 00:09:14,000
one second two three

236
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,366
the kind of silence that has weight

237
00:09:16,366 --> 00:09:18,300
that has teeth are you hurt

238
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,266
Min June's voice was so calm

239
00:09:20,266 --> 00:09:22,000
it circled back to terrifying

240
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,600
not a raised syllable not a single crack

241
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:27,866
just ice stretching in every direction

242
00:09:27,866 --> 00:09:30,366
I'm okay just a scratch

243
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,466
don't lie to me Amara

244
00:09:32,466 --> 00:09:34,600
my elbow is bleeding I fell

245
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,700
but I'm who touched you

246
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:40,700
she closed her eyes who touched you

247
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,266
my ex fiance Marcus

248
00:09:44,266 --> 00:09:46,533
but security has him it's

249
00:09:46,766 --> 00:09:48,600
I'm 10 minutes away minion

250
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:51,500
please don't he put his hands on you

251
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,966
still calm still ice

252
00:09:53,966 --> 00:09:57,000
he hurt you there is no version of this

253
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,600
where he walks away without consequences

254
00:09:59,633 --> 00:10:02,266
the line went dead Amara looked at Jean Wu

255
00:10:02,266 --> 00:10:04,700
pinning Marcus to the polished marble floor

256
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,166
at Taiyang standing guard beside her

257
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:10,100
with the expression of a man watching a fuse burn

258
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:13,400
at Marcus's girlfriend screaming at security guards

259
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:16,100
at the crowd of shoppers with their phones out

260
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:17,700
recording whispering

261
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,933
and she felt it settle in her stomach

262
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:23,100
cold certain inevitable

263
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:25,600
Marcus had no idea what he'd done

264
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,366
Min John arrived in eight minutes

265
00:10:27,366 --> 00:10:29,700
it took him six of those to cross Gangnam

266
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:32,900
in a black motorcade that ran three red lights

267
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,633
he spent the other two sitting in the parking garage

268
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:37,033
gripping the steering wheel

269
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:38,666
until his knuckles turned white

270
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:40,466
breathing through the kind of rage

271
00:10:40,466 --> 00:10:43,066
that made men do things they couldn't take back

272
00:10:43,066 --> 00:10:44,566
he thought about his father

273
00:10:44,566 --> 00:10:46,300
he thought about the sound of his mother

274
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,700
crying through a locked door

275
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:50,100
he thought about Amara's voice on the phone

276
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:53,800
small shaking trying to protect him from himself

277
00:10:53,966 --> 00:10:56,166
by saying she was fine and

278
