556
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
you're not going back to that school

557
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,166
it's not safe anymore your face is everywhere

558
00:21:53,166 --> 00:21:54,800
I'll increase security here

559
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:57,133
and no he stopped

560
00:21:57,166 --> 00:21:59,866
not used to the word not from her Amara

561
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:03,233
I lost everything once because I depended on a man

562
00:22:03,233 --> 00:22:05,800
she stood and her voice didn't shake

563
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:08,900
not even a little and she was proud of that

564
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,633
my money my home

565
00:22:10,633 --> 00:22:12,166
my baby everything

566
00:22:12,166 --> 00:22:15,733
because I built my entire life around someone else

567
00:22:15,766 --> 00:22:18,833
and when he left there was nothing underneath

568
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:21,133
she looked at him I won't do that again

569
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:24,400
not even for you not even for someone I love

570
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,066
this is about your safety

571
00:22:26,066 --> 00:22:28,166
this is about my identity

572
00:22:28,166 --> 00:22:30,833
that job is mine I fought for it

573
00:22:30,833 --> 00:22:33,433
and I'll fight to keep it on my own terms

574
00:22:33,433 --> 00:22:35,366
I can make one phone call

575
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,766
that's exactly the problem Minjin

576
00:22:37,833 --> 00:22:40,400
you can always make one phone call

577
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,400
and every time you do I become smaller

578
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,366
less mine more yours

579
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:46,833
he flinched actually

580
00:22:46,833 --> 00:22:48,900
flinched as if she'd struck him

581
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:51,100
the silence stretched between them

582
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,966
not comfortable not charged

583
00:22:52,966 --> 00:22:53,866
just heavy

584
00:22:53,866 --> 00:22:56,233
the weight of two people who loved each other

585
00:22:56,233 --> 00:22:57,566
standing on opposite sides

586
00:22:57,566 --> 00:22:59,300
of something that couldn't be solved

587
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:01,866
with money or power or violence

588
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:03,500
he left without another word

589
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:06,966
the door closed softly somehow worse than a slam

590
00:23:06,966 --> 00:23:08,866
Amara sat on the kitchen floor

591
00:23:08,866 --> 00:23:11,166
back against the island and cried

592
00:23:11,166 --> 00:23:12,833
not because she was scared

593
00:23:12,833 --> 00:23:14,500
because she loved him so much

594
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:16,400
it was rearranging her bones

595
00:23:16,666 --> 00:23:18,400
and she knew knew

596
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,833
with the certainty of a woman

597
00:23:19,833 --> 00:23:22,666
who'd already survived one devastating loss

598
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,200
that love was not enough if it came with a cage

599
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,366
even a golden one

600
00:23:27,366 --> 00:23:29,733
even one built with the best intentions

601
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:31,300
he didn't come home that night

602
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:31,500
and

603
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:34,400
for the first time since she'd married Kong Min June

604
00:23:34,733 --> 00:23:37,333
Amara slept alone in their enormous bed

605
00:23:37,466 --> 00:23:39,566
and wondered if loving a king

606
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,866
meant she would always be a subject

607
00:23:41,866 --> 00:23:43,666
he came back at 3 in the morning

608
00:23:43,666 --> 00:23:45,033
she heard the front door

609
00:23:45,033 --> 00:23:47,400
the soft click of his shoes on the hardwood

610
00:23:47,400 --> 00:23:49,466
the clink of a glass whiskey

611
00:23:49,466 --> 00:23:50,366
probably

612
00:23:50,433 --> 00:23:53,700
the Yamazaki 18 he kept on the shelf by the window

613
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:57,233
then silence she found him on the balcony

614
00:23:57,233 --> 00:23:58,666
sitting on the concrete floor

615
00:23:58,666 --> 00:24:00,366
with his back against the railing

616
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,800
his legs stretched out the glass balanced on his knee

617
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:06,533
the city shimmered 42 stories below

618
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:08,500
soul dressed in Christmas lights

619
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:10,500
gold and white and endless

620
00:24:10,500 --> 00:24:12,666
he looked up when she stepped outside

621
00:24:12,666 --> 00:24:15,300
his eyes were red she didn't say anything

622
00:24:15,366 --> 00:24:16,600
just sat beside him

623
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:18,500
close enough that their shoulders touched

624
00:24:18,500 --> 00:24:20,800
the silence lasted a long time

625
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:23,366
long enough for the cold to seep through her robe

626
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:24,966
for her breath to cloud

627
00:24:24,966 --> 00:24:26,900
for the ice in his glass to melt

628
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:30,566
then quietly so quietly she almost missed it

629
00:24:30,566 --> 00:24:33,700
he said my father used to hit my mother

630
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:36,533
Amara went still not often

631
00:24:36,633 --> 00:24:39,166
not he laughed hollow

632
00:24:39,166 --> 00:24:40,500
not like you think

633
00:24:40,766 --> 00:24:43,500
he wasn't a drunk who beat his wife every Saturday

634
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:46,000
he was a powerful man who loved her

635
00:24:46,233 --> 00:24:48,700
truly loved her and still

636
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:50,000
couldn't stop the violence

637
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:52,400
from leaking into everything he touched

638
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:55,466
it would happen once maybe twice a year

639
00:24:55,466 --> 00:24:58,166
always after something went wrong in the business

640
00:24:58,166 --> 00:25:02,366
always followed by gifts jewelry trips apologies

641
00:25:02,366 --> 00:25:05,066
she always forgave him he stared at the skyline

642
00:25:05,066 --> 00:25:07,300
I was 8 the first time I saw it

643
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:09,700
hid under my bed and Learned two things

644
00:25:09,700 --> 00:25:12,366
that love isn't enough to make a man safe

645
00:25:12,366 --> 00:25:15,833
and that power corrupts even the purest intentions

646
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:18,400
Amara's throat ached Min Jun

647
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:20,233
I'm terrified Amara

648
00:25:20,233 --> 00:25:22,266
his voice cracked on her name

649
00:25:22,266 --> 00:25:24,833
the first crack she'd ever heard in Kong

650
00:25:24,833 --> 00:25:27,966
Min Jun's voice I'm terrified I'm becoming him

651
00:25:27,966 --> 00:25:30,233
I looked at myself in the mirror last night

652
00:25:30,233 --> 00:25:32,500
and saw his face his hands

653
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:35,200
I broke that man's ribs and I felt

654
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:37,500
he stopped swallowed

655
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:40,166
I felt calm I felt right

656
00:25:40,166 --> 00:25:43,666
and that scares me more than any enemy I've ever had

657
00:25:43,666 --> 00:25:45,700
she reached over and took his hand

658
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:48,433
the bruised one she held it between both of hers

659
00:25:48,433 --> 00:25:51,433
and pressed it to her chest over her heartbeat

660
00:25:51,433 --> 00:25:53,266
tell me about yours he whispered

661
00:25:53,266 --> 00:25:56,600
then looking at her tell me about the things you carry

662
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:58,366
I want to know all of it

663
00:25:58,366 --> 00:26:01,033
everything you've been holding alone

664
00:26:01,033 --> 00:26:03,166
so she told him about Marcus

665
00:26:03,166 --> 00:26:04,866
about the note on the counter

666
00:26:04,866 --> 00:26:07,566
about coming home to an empty apartment

667
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:09,333
and an empty bank account

668
00:26:09,466 --> 00:26:13,833
and standing in a painted nursery with $17 to her name

669
00:26:13,833 --> 00:26:15,400
about living in her car

670
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:18,066
about trying to eat enough to keep the baby alive

671
00:26:18,066 --> 00:26:18,900
and failing

672
00:26:18,900 --> 00:26:21,966
about waking in a pool of blood on a shelter floor

673
00:26:22,166 --> 00:26:24,600
and driving herself to the emergency room

674
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:26,366
because there was no one to call

675
00:26:26,366 --> 00:26:27,900
about hope I named her

676
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:30,166
Amara's voice was barely a sound

677
00:26:30,166 --> 00:26:32,466
I know they said it was too early to know

678
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:35,000
but I knew she was a girl

679
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:38,800
and I named her hope because that's what she was

680
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:40,966
the last thing I had left

681
00:26:40,966 --> 00:26:44,166
her breath hitched I've never told anyone her name

682
00:26:44,166 --> 00:26:47,366
Min June's jaw trembled he turned his hand in hers

683
00:26:47,566 --> 00:26:49,266
laced their fingers together

684
00:26:49,266 --> 00:26:51,400
tell me about hope he whispered

685
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:54,266
in the way he said the name like it was holy

686
00:26:54,266 --> 00:26:57,466
like it mattered like their daughter had been real

687
00:26:57,466 --> 00:26:58,700
and not just a ghost

688
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:01,266
Amara had carried alone for three years

689
00:27:01,533 --> 00:27:03,300
broke something open inside her

690
00:27:03,300 --> 00:27:06,066
that she'd welded shut the night she lost everything

691
00:27:06,100 --> 00:27:08,600
their daughter he said their daughter

692
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,666
not your baby not what happened

693
00:27:10,666 --> 00:27:13,200
their daughter as if hope belonged to both of them

694
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:15,500
as if he'd claimed her across time

695
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:18,266
across all the years he hadn't been there

696
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:21,433
across the impossibility of loving a child

697
00:27:21,433 --> 00:27:24,600
he'd never known existed until this moment

698
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,166
she told him everything

699
00:27:26,166 --> 00:27:28,133
the color she'd painted the nursery

700
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:30,100
soft yellow like morning

701
00:27:30,100 --> 00:27:32,200
the onesie she'd bought at a thrift store

702
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,266
with daisies on it

703
00:27:33,266 --> 00:27:35,666
the way she'd talk to her stomach at night

704
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:38,733
telling hope about the world she'd be born into

705
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:41,166
making promises she couldn't keep

706
00:27:41,166 --> 00:27:43,900
Minjun listened he didn't try to fix it

707
00:27:43,966 --> 00:27:46,666
didn't offer solutions or platitudes

708
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:49,233
or the kind of hollow comfort that people give

709
00:27:49,233 --> 00:27:50,966
when they don't know what else to say

710
00:27:50,966 --> 00:27:52,800
he just held her hand and listened

711
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:56,033
and let her voice crack and shake and go silent

712
00:27:56,033 --> 00:27:58,600
and come back again and when she was done

713
00:27:58,633 --> 00:28:00,766
when there was nothing left to say

714
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,433
he did something that undid her completely

715
00:28:03,433 --> 00:28:05,300
he leaned his head against her shoulder

716
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:06,966
Kong Min Jun underground

717
00:28:06,966 --> 00:28:07,866
king of soul

718
00:28:07,866 --> 00:28:11,700
the man who made powerful men tremble with a phone call

719
00:28:11,700 --> 00:28:14,566
the man whose hands had broken bones that afternoon

720
00:28:14,566 --> 00:28:15,633
without a tremor

721
00:28:15,633 --> 00:28:18,233
he rested his head on her shoulder like a child

722
00:28:18,233 --> 00:28:19,633
like the eight year old boy

723
00:28:19,633 --> 00:28:22,266
who'd hidden under his bed and never been held

724
00:28:22,266 --> 00:28:24,866
afterward she wrapped her arms around him

725
00:28:24,866 --> 00:28:26,466
pressed her lips to his hair

726
00:28:26,466 --> 00:28:28,366
and they sat there on that balcony

727
00:28:28,433 --> 00:28:32,100
42 stories above a city that belonged to him

728
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:33,566
and cried together

729
00:28:33,566 --> 00:28:35,366
they didn't fix each other that night

730
00:28:35,366 --> 00:28:37,000
that's not how healing works

731
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:40,100
but they did something harder and more important

732
00:28:40,100 --> 00:28:42,566
they stopped pretending they didn't need fixing

733
00:28:42,566 --> 00:28:44,100
things changed after that

734
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:46,366
not all at once not dramatically

735
00:28:46,466 --> 00:28:49,333
the way seasons change slowly

736
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:52,966
then all at once until you look up and realize

737
00:28:52,966 --> 00:28:55,300
the entire landscape is different

738
00:28:56,100 --> 00:28:58,566
Amara went to the school meeting alone

739
00:28:58,566 --> 00:29:00,566
no bodyguards in the parking lot

740
00:29:00,633 --> 00:29:03,300
no phone calls from Min Jun to the headmaster

741
00:29:03,300 --> 00:29:05,500
she sat across from three administrators

742
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:07,100
and two concerned parents

743
00:29:07,100 --> 00:29:09,666
and defended herself with her teaching record

744
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:13,133
her evaluations her students'test scores

745
00:29:13,366 --> 00:29:16,433
and the quiet unshakable dignity of a woman

746
00:29:16,433 --> 00:29:19,366
who had survived far worse than a PTA complaint

747
00:29:19,366 --> 00:29:22,566
she kept her job she hired her own lawyer

748
00:29:22,566 --> 00:29:24,000
not one of Min Jun's

749
00:29:24,033 --> 00:29:26,200
a young woman named Yoon Hee AE jin

750
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:28,500
from a midsize firm in Mapogu

751
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:30,633
who specialized in nonprofit law

752
00:29:30,633 --> 00:29:32,800
together they began building the framework

753
00:29:32,800 --> 00:29:34,700
for what Amara had been dreaming about

754
00:29:34,700 --> 00:29:36,300
since the night on the balcony

755
00:29:36,766 --> 00:29:39,266
the Second Chances Foundation housing

756
00:29:39,266 --> 00:29:41,033
job training therapy

757
00:29:41,033 --> 00:29:44,800
childcare everything she'd wished for and never had

758
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:47,166
this was hers built with her vision

759
00:29:47,166 --> 00:29:48,866
her pain her name

760
00:29:48,866 --> 00:29:51,500
minjin watched he didn't interfere

761
00:29:51,500 --> 00:29:53,000
it was she knew

762
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,066
the hardest thing he'd ever done

763
00:29:55,466 --> 00:29:57,800
harder than any business negotiation

764
00:29:57,833 --> 00:30:01,200
any territorial dispute any act of violence

765
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:03,066
standing back letting her lead

766
00:30:03,066 --> 00:30:05,400
but he was learning when Park Jay sung

767
00:30:05,433 --> 00:30:06,066
a rival

768
00:30:06,066 --> 00:30:09,066
who'd sent veiled threats after the video went viral

769
00:30:09,166 --> 00:30:10,933
escalated his provocations

770
00:30:11,600 --> 00:30:13,666
Min Jun didn't reach for violence

771
00:30:13,700 --> 00:30:16,500
he reached for strategy bought out Park's debt

772
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:20,000
turned an enemy into a debtor with a single transaction

773
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:20,866
and a smile

774
00:30:20,866 --> 00:30:23,633
that was somehow more terrifying than a fist

775
00:30:23,633 --> 00:30:26,166
when Amara asked did you hurt anyone

776
00:30:26,166 --> 00:30:29,166
he looked at her with something new in his eyes

777
00:30:29,166 --> 00:30:31,300
something that might have been pride or

778
00:30:31,300 --> 00:30:34,233
or maybe just relief no

779
00:30:34,233 --> 00:30:35,866
you asked me to be better

780
00:30:35,866 --> 00:30:36,933
I'm trying

781
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,433
trying is enough she said

782
00:30:39,433 --> 00:30:41,433
for now he almost smiled

783
00:30:41,433 --> 00:30:42,333
for now

784
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:46,066
Marcus's public apology came on a Tuesday

785
00:30:46,066 --> 00:30:47,633
Amara watched it on her phone

786
00:30:47,633 --> 00:30:49,400
during her lunch break at school

787
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:51,166
sitting in the faculty room

788
00:30:51,166 --> 00:30:52,766
with a cup of instant coffee

789
00:30:52,766 --> 00:30:55,433
and a kimbap from the convenience store downstairs

790
00:30:55,433 --> 00:30:57,266
Marcus looked hollowed out

791
00:30:57,266 --> 00:31:00,000
broken in the specific way that men break

792
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,266
when the world finally holds them accountable

793
00:31:02,266 --> 00:31:03,566
he read from a script

794
00:31:03,566 --> 00:31:06,600
she recognized Min Jun's precision in every sentence

795
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:09,700
and apologize to her to the other women

796
00:31:09,700 --> 00:31:11,866
to the public she felt nothing

797
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:14,566
not satisfaction not pity

798
00:31:14,566 --> 00:31:17,066
not anger just nothing

799
00:31:17,066 --> 00:31:18,800
she deleted the notification

800
00:31:18,966 --> 00:31:20,000
finished her kimbap

801
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,166
and went back to teaching her 3rd graders

802
00:31:22,166 --> 00:31:25,166
the difference between past tense and present perfect

803
00:31:25,166 --> 00:31:28,766
the past was past she was living in the present

804
00:31:28,766 --> 00:31:30,300
and for the first time

805
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:32,866
the present didn't feel like a place she was hiding in

806
00:31:32,866 --> 00:31:35,033
a week later Marcus sent an email

807
00:31:35,033 --> 00:31:36,666
she read it standing in the kitchen

808
00:31:36,666 --> 00:31:38,500
while Minjun made bulgogi

809
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:40,600
he'd been taking cooking classes

810
00:31:40,666 --> 00:31:42,533
badly endearingly

811
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:44,366
burning the garlic every time

812
00:31:44,366 --> 00:31:47,166
but refusing to give up the email was short

813
00:31:47,166 --> 00:31:49,100
I saw the news about your foundation

814
00:31:49,100 --> 00:31:51,500
I'm proud of you you deserved better than me

815
00:31:51,500 --> 00:31:52,766
and I'm glad you found it

816
00:31:52,766 --> 00:31:53,800
she read it once

817
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:57,166
felt the last locked door inside her chest swing open

818
00:31:57,566 --> 00:32:00,200
letting in light she didn't know she'd been blocking

819
00:32:00,266 --> 00:32:02,633
then she deleted it who was that

820
00:32:02,633 --> 00:32:05,800
Min Jun asked scraping burnt garlic into the trash

821
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:07,200
with the resigned expression

822
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:09,533
of a man who controlled an empire

823
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:12,066
but could not control a stove top

824
00:32:12,066 --> 00:32:13,566
nobody she said

825
00:32:13,566 --> 00:32:15,233
and meant it that night

826
00:32:15,233 --> 00:32:17,900
he gave her the necklace a delicate gold chain

827
00:32:17,900 --> 00:32:19,833
with a pendant shaped like a Phoenix

828
00:32:19,833 --> 00:32:22,766
rising from flames wings spread

829
00:32:22,766 --> 00:32:26,700
head lifted every feather etched with impossible detail

830
00:32:26,700 --> 00:32:29,400
you rose from the ashes he said softly

831
00:32:29,566 --> 00:32:31,266
fastening it around her neck

